 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to direct the department of civil service to study certain\nairport-related titles",
    "basePrintNo": "S9102",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9102-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9102\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to direct the department of civil service to study certain\nairport-related titles\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require the Department of Civil Service to conduct a study on the\nCivil Service classification of aviation positions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Directs the Department of Civil Service airport-related\ntitles in the civil service of the civil service commissions.to conduct\na study on state and in all municipal\n\nSection 2: Requires the Department to complete the after the enactment\nof this legislation.study within 180 days\n\nSection 3: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nModern airports require a variety of specialized aviation personnel to\nrun safely and effectively. Due to New York Civil Service requirements,\nairports are required to hire employees on a provisional basis for these\npositions until they complete the requirements to become full employees.\nThis provisional hiring makes it difficult for New York airports,\nparticularly Upstate airports to find qualified candidates. There is a\nlimited national pool of candidates for these positions and they are\noften lost to different airports that do not have to hire on a provi-\nsional basis. It has made it difficult for New York airports to recruit\nessential aviation staff.\n\nThis legislation will direct the Department of Civil Service to conduct\na study on the classification of aviation positions in New York. The\ngoal is to have the Department identify which positions should be\nreclassified to ensure airports can effectively recruit candidates for\nthese positions.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
